# Notification unsubscribe links: an earlier comparison failure and its correction

This document records a comparison failure found in earlier versions of the
port, the correction made for it, and the latest comparison result. The
reference runtime is Ruby 3.2.3 on the project's Linux VM (Decko 0.20.0 /
card 1.110.0), and the fixture's committed recorded Ruby outputs for
synthetic-v1 were captured there on 2026-11-03. The earlier failure and the
first two passing results below were graded against the recording those
outputs replaced, a 2026-10-08 capture taken on Windows with Ruby 3.3.12; the
two differ only in class-token order (rule N3) and random slot ids (rule N1).
The exact source of this package is named by sourceCommit and
engineCommit in HANDOVER-MANIFEST.json, which is generated at export. The
results below describe their named development snapshots, not an automatic
grade of a combined source or exported artifact.

## Latest result

The current recorded SQLite synthetic-v1 comparison passes rendering
1754/1754, semantics 2389/2389, persistence 16/16 and side effects 19/19 on
the source snapshot listed in EVIDENCE.md. The native MySQL main-fixture
comparison also passes all four categories against a fresh stock Ruby 3.2.3
reference capture. These results retain the notification-link correction.
The renamed synthetic-v2 comparison now passes too: its 24 previously
differing email-page answers reproduce Ruby's actual missing-codename errors;
they are not 24 remaining mismatches.

The complete mod-write probe still fails on persistence, side effects and
